pe":"text"},{"text":"shortest-path predecessor of ","type":"text"},{"code":"v","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" settled first. Vertices at equal distance settle in an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"unspecified order, so when several vertices at the same smallest distance lead to ","type":"text"},{"code":"v","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" along","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"shortest paths, which one is the parent is unspecified. Among parallel edges from the parent,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the parent edge is the cheapest, and the first in ","type":"text"},{"code":"outEdges(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" order among equals.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A tree holds a copy of the graph, so looking a vertex up never hashes on a representation"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with cheap vertex indices. While the tree is alive, the next mutation of the original copies"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it; a tree of a graph about to change should be read and dropped first."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"With several sources, each starts at distance zero ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".one"},{"type":"text","text":" over a semiring) with no parent."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Dijkstra’s algorithm and breadth-first search never improve on that, so a source keeps no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"parent even when another source reaches it. Bellman–Ford treats the sources as one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"super-source: a negative path from one source to another improves the second, which then"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"has that distance, a parent and a path from the first."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Over a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SelectiveSemiring"},{"text":" a distance is the ⊗-product of a path’s weights, the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"best by the natural order ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"<"},{"text":", and a vertex is reached exactly when its distance is not ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".zero"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Not "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Equatable"},{"type":"text","text":": two correct trees can choose different parents on ties."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"references":{"doc://ShortestPaths/documentation/ShortestPaths/ShortestPathTree/distance(to:)":{"role":"symbol","title":"distance(to:)","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/ShortestPathTree\/distance(to:)","url":"\/documentation\/shortestpaths\/shortestpathtree\/distance(to:)","abstract":[{"text":"The length of a shortest path from a source to ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertex","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", or ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" when no path reaches it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(or every path is longer than the cutoff).","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"distance","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"to","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"G","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P6VertexQa"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Distance","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://ShortestPaths/documentation/ShortestPaths/ShortestPathTree/distance(checkedTo:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/shortestpaths\/shortestpathtree\/distance(checkedto:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/ShortestPathTree\/distance(checkedTo:)","kind":"symbol","conform